 in a draw, both passed at 0.0 after a game with no blunders; Opus 5.5 averaged 1.4 points lost per move and the 12k 1.3. White built an early edge, with Black's lead down at -4.5 by move 7, but the center fights through moves 14 to 18 gave it back. The middle game was then a run of 4 to 5 point swings from moves 22 to 27. Each side kept playing elsewhere while the D9/C9 corner went untouched, and once Opus 5.5 played D9 on move 28 the game stayed level to the end.", "moments": [{"turn": 14, "text": "Opus 5.5's E4 pushed against the Black wall on the F-file and lost 3.2 points, the engine preferring F3. It was the first sign the early White edge was starting to leak."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "C7 lost 4.0 points while the engine wanted F2. White's lead of 3.9 on the board turned into 0.1 in Black's favor, as the F2/E2 area was left to Black."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "Opus 5.5 played H5 on the right side, losing 4.5 points. The engine's choice was D9, in the top-left corner, and the move turned Black's lead from 0.1 into 4.6."}, {"turn": 24, "text": "H3 was Opus 5.5's worst move of the game at 5.4 points lost, again with the engine's eye on C9. It stretched White along the H-file instead of settling the corner."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "The 12k answered with H2, which also lost 5.4 points and brought the lead back from 5.4 to 0.0. Both worst moves of the game came in this exchange, each side ignoring the same corner."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "Opus 5.5 finally played D9, the engine's choice, at no cost. C9 and the E9/D1/C1/E1 exchanges followed, and the score stayed at 0.0 through the final passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and flood-fills each group to print its stones and liberty count, flagging groups with two or fewer liberties; it ranks no moves and looks ahead no further than the current position, so it is a board-inspection helper.", "stop": false}}